# Kademi controllers.xml

This file is the app manifest. Two things about it cause most of the confusion:

- **`engineVersion` on the root `<controllers>` element decides the JS engine, for the whole app.**
  `2.0` means GraalJS and `.mjs`; `1.1` or no attribute means Nashorn and `.js`. You do not get to
  choose per file, and a `.mjs` file in a `1.1` app is simply never loaded.
- **A script file only loads if it is listed as a `<source>`.** Adding a file to `APP-INF/` is not
  enough. Under GraalJS, declare the single `app.mjs` entrypoint and let it `import` the rest;
  under Nashorn, list every file, and order matters because there are no modules.

Everything else - controllers, services, portlets, components, queries, event listeners - is
registered from JS by calling methods on the `controllerMappings` global, not declared here.

Changing `engineVersion` on an existing app is a rewrite of every script file in it.

Full guidance: the `kademi-server-js` skill, and its `references/controllers-xml.md`.
